            },
            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 12,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Oliver Brewka",
                        "email": "oliver.brewka@9elements.com",
                        "username": "mox669"
                    },
                    "message": "These helpers were already put into a seperate utility file. Since these helpers partially run on single-host aswell, calling the file 'multi_host' might be a bit misleading. Also, looking at the current file structure, splitting this into hpp and cpp files does not align with the rest of the repo."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 12,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "> Also, looking at the current file structure, splitting this into hpp and cpp files does not align with the rest of the repo.\n\nImplementing functions in headers when they don't need to be there is an antipattern. Refer to https://isocpp.github.io/CppCoreGuidelines/CppCoreGuidelines#sf2-a-header-file-must-not-contain-object-definitions-or-non-inline-function-definitions\n\nAnd marking things `inline` does not necessarily makes things faster or smaller.\nhttps://isocpp.org/wiki/faq/inline-functions\n\nIt's probably just a waste of time to do that and makes the build slower.\n\n\n\n> calling the file 'multi_host' might be a bit misleading.\n\nI wanted to have a separate file for Ed to be able to throw out in case the code does not develop into something worthwhile."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 12,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "> calling the file 'multi_host' might be a bit misleading.\n\nFrom my perspective single-host is just a special case of a multi-host system (number of hosts == 1). So i think it is fine to have this filename.\n\nOfc in bmcweb things are not so simple but i still think the name is ok.\n\nAnd we get a separate translation unit which can potentially speed up the build."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 17,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Oliver Brewka",
                        "email": "oliver.brewka@9elements.com",
                        "username": "mox669"
                    },
                    "message": "Not exactly sure what this means. I have updated the expiry date of the option flag, prior of knowing that we might stick to it permanently. As such, these helpers probably won't be removed aswell."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 17,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "This is a tough one since usually people don't allow merging code that has no callers / users.\n\nI wrote this with the expectation that the callers would be merged soon after this patch. If that does not happen for whatever reason this is essentially dead code, and dead code will simply be removed (after some time)."
                }
            ],
